# Dialog close button

Native `<dialog>` / modal panels use a shared close control that sits **outside** the panel so it never covers content.

## Markup

```html
<dialog class="app-dialog some-dialog">
  <button type="button" class="app-dialog-close" aria-label="Kapat" data-*-close></button>
  <div class="…-sheet"><!-- scrollable content --></div>
</dialog>
```

- Empty button body — **no** `×` / `&times;` / SVG / text
- Always include `aria-label="Kapat"` (or locale equivalent)
- Prefer `data-*-close` for the click handler hook
- Put `.app-dialog` on the `<dialog>` (with any page-specific class)

## Visual

- Class: `.app-dialog-close` (defined in `scss/_components.scss`)
- X is drawn with `::before` / `::after` bars only
- Anchored to the **right** of the dialog (`left: calc(100% + 20px)`, `top: 0`) — 20px gap
- `border-radius: 0` (square)
- Keep dialog `overflow: visible`; scroll the inner sheet instead
- Reserve horizontal room in the dialog `max-width` so the control stays in the viewport (`20px` + close width)

## Do not

- Place the close control inside a header that eats content space
- Place it above the dialog
- Use border-radius on the close button
- Use a glyph or icon font for the X
- Clip the button with `overflow: hidden` on the dialog
